JOB PURPOSE:
This role provides specialized nutrition and dietetic support for oncology patients receiving care at Medserve–LUTH Cancer Centre.
The Dietician will assess nutritional needs, develop individualized nutrition care plans, and provide evidence-based dietary interventions to support cancer treatment, recovery, symptom management, and quality of life. The role operates on a Part-time basis, with scheduled on-site clinical support as required.
JOB RESPONSIBILITIES
Conduct comprehensive nutritional assessments for oncology patients;
Develop, implement, and monitor individualized nutrition care plans aligned with cancer treatment protocols;
Provide dietary counselling to manage treatment-related side effects such as weight loss, malnutrition, nausea, fatigue, and appetite changes;
Support patients before, during, and after chemotherapy, radiotherapy, and other cancer treatments;
Deliver virtual and in-person consultations in line with the Centre’s hybrid care model;
Collaborate closely with oncologists, radiation therapists, nurses, and other healthcare professionals to ensure holistic patient care;
Educate patients and caregivers on therapeutic nutrition, meal planning, and lifestyle modification;
Monitor patient progress and update nutrition plans based on clinical outcomes;
Maintain accurate, confidential, and up-to-date patient records in compliance with hospital policies;
Ensure adherence to professional ethics, patient confidentiality, and healthcare regulations;
Participate in multidisciplinary team meetings and case discussions where required;
Contribute to patient education programs, wellness initiatives, and cancer support services;
Participate in quality improvement activities, audits, or clinical reviews related to nutrition services where required;
Keep informed on advancements in oncology nutrition and evidence-based practice;
Perform administrative duties and clinical documentation as required.
JOB REQUIREMENTS
Ability to work independently and manage clinical workload effectively;
Ability to function as part of a multidisciplinary oncology team;
Excellent communication and counselling skills;
High level of professionalism when handling sensitive and confidential patient information;
Strong organizational and documentation skills;
Proficiency in Microsoft Office tools and virtual consultation platforms;
In addition to the above;
A minimum of 6 years post-qualification experience is required;
A degree in Dietetics, Nutrition, or a related field is required;

Overview
Jhpiego seeks a MEL Specialist for the “Quality Improvement and Leadership and Management Strengthening through Technical Assistance” project implemented in four states. The project aims to provide support to Global Fund programs in Nigeria to implement an innovative approach for integrated supportive supervision (ISS) that includes collaborative improvement, training, a web-enabled supervision checklist, and supervision of supervisors to improve health worker performance and quality of care for integrated HIV/TB/Malaria/COVID19 and Community services. The MEL Specialist will be responsible to gather, analyze, and process complex information related to all aspects of program activity implementation. S/he will conduct impact assessments, baseline studies, surveys and need assessments to identify necessary changes and future project opportunities. He/She will be responsible for ensuring that lessons learned are integrated into project implementation to continuously improve quality of interventions and outcomes. Also, will be responsible for ensuring the timeliness and quality of data, working closely with the State Ministry of Health, LGA, health facilities and communities and with the QI specialist/advisor and MEL specialist per state
Responsibilities
Contribute to reporting on Project Monitoring and Evaluation Plan (PMEP), including review of its theory of change, results framework, identify indicators, relevant and applicable baseline data collection strategies and methodologies, and resources needed to successfully implement the MEL strategy;
Ensure accurate, high quality data are routinely collected and entered into the Project Monitoring Information System to track project specific indicators;
Mentor and supervise health workers in the use of tools for data collection and protocols for performance monitoring as well as baseline, midline and end line and other assessments as needed;
Ensure accurate, high quality data are routinely collected and entered into JADE to track Jhpiego impact goal indicators;
Support strategic collaboration activities with MoH, key stakeholders at LGA and facilities to learn from evidence generated by the project, and adapt interventions as appropriate;
Support project deliverables with a focus on M&E sections;
Support Government in strengthening integrated health data management processes
Ensure measurement of QI project activities and milestones including contrbution to results
Provide M&E summaries for the project at state level, including presentation of updates to key stakeholders;
Analyze and make data available for QI projects at State level and LGA
Ensure use of data visualization tool
Ensure data collected are uploaded to Creative web-based platform;
Analyze ongoing quantitative / qualitative data at different points in the program leading to the specific program / contract results;
Collaborate with the QI technical team to monitor the progress of the program in terms of the compliance requirements of Global Fund results and indicators;
Provide hands on MEL QI support to health facilities including leadership and management team
Work closely with technical staff and institutional partners to explain MEL processes and understand how these processes relate to the project's technical work, and to promote MEL-related training as needed;
Other related duties as assigned.
Required Qualifications
Bachelor's Degree in Social sciences, Public Health or related field, and equivalent job experience over 6years' in programmatic support of international health projects (Doctors, Nurses, medical degree added advantage)
MPH and Masters of Science in health services, statistics and others health related field
Strong familiarity with health system and HIV, TB, COVID19, Community interventions and Malaria service delivery context in supported states
Ability to interact with established networks of senior level international health professionals, ministry of health officials and other partners
Comfortable with a team approach to programming and the ability to manage several major activities simultaneously
Ability to travel 60% of time and supported LGAs, communities and facilities
Proficiency in word processing, Microsoft Office
